{{also|Perkele}}
==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*perkeleh}}. Derives from the name of the {{der|fi|bat}} deity of thunder; compare {{cog|lt|Perkūnas}} and {{cog|sla-pro|*Perunъ}}. <br /> After Finland's conquest (c. 1250) and subsequent Christianization, its meaning changed to a profanity and a euphemism for Satan at least partly due to the influence of the clergy.

